# Command
Interactive wizard for adding commands to plugins.
## Instructions
### Phase 1: Context Detection
Detect plugin (find plugin.json) or list available plugins.
### Phase 2: Command Discovery
Read command architecture:
```
Read: ${JSTACK_PLUGIN_ROOT}/references/organizational-guides/command-architecture.md
```
### Phase 3: Configuration
Ask user:
1. **Command name** (kebab-case)
2. **Command type** (wizard|generator|orchestrator|utility)
3. **Purpose** (one sentence; does a public skill already carry this intent?)
4. **Arguments** (yes/no, format)
5. **Tool permissions** (Read, Write, Bash, etc)
6. **Workflow** (type-specific questions)
### Phase 4: Template Selection
Based on type, read template:
```
Read: ${JSTACK_PLUGIN_ROOT}/references/templates/{type}-command-template.md
```
### Phase 5: Generation
Create `commands/{name}.md`:
```markdown
---
description: {purpose, at most 60 columns}
argument: {true|false}
allowed-tools: {tools}
---
# /{name} — {hint}
{Instructions based on template}
```
Drop the `description` line when a public skill carries the intent or the
command only invokes a skill. Such a command is not listed to the model, so it
costs nothing against the listing budget (about 1% of the context window), and
its first body line, `# /{name} — {hint}`, is the text the `/` menu shows. Omit
the key rather than leave it empty: `description:` with no value fails
validation. `disable-model-invocation` is reserved for workflows the model must
never start.
### Phase 6: Integration
- Update plugin.json keywords
- Create supporting scripts if needed
- Update commands README
### Phase 7: Validation
```bash
!bash ${JSTACK_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/validate_plugin.js .
```
### Phase 8: Completion
Show summary and next steps:
- Test command
- Add hook/agent
- Validate plugin
## Quality Checks
- [PASS] Name follows conventions
- [PASS] YAML frontmatter valid
- [PASS] Description at most 60 columns, or absent because a skill carries the intent
- [PASS] Instructions complete
- [OK] Command ready
